From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max rossi <113717219+maxr0ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] wined3d: Keep managed textures' system memory in host
 memory under WoW64.

d3d8/9 build a managed texture from two wined3d textures: a CPU-only one the application maps and
a GPU-only one draws use. The CPU-only one never gives its system memory up, so in a 32-bit
process every byte of managed texture costs a byte of the 2 GiB address space for as long as the
texture lives (measured: 1.03 bytes per byte for 1024x1024 DXT5; a process runs out after ~1.85 GiB
of such textures), while the GPU copy costs nothing there: the host driver keeps it above 4 GiB.

When the application has filled a managed texture (the unmap of its last sub-resource) and after
every upload, copy its system memory into a host allocation through wined3d.so, free the 32-bit
copy and mark the sub-resources discarded. Loading or preparing a system memory location copies
it back first: the upload at the first draw and after EvictManagedResources() (the texture is
stashed again right after), an application map, GetDC(). A texture mapped again after a stash
stays in system memory from then on. The bytes an application reads back are the ones it wrote;
nothing is read back from GL. Measured: 3 GiB of 1024x1024 DXT5 managed textures in 14 MiB of
address space. WINED3D_STASH_MANAGED=0 disables it; so does a missing wined3d.so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
